6. STEP 5 – CREATE JKS DIRECTLY FROM CMP PFX
===============================================================================

Once the PFX is validated, create the application JKS directly from the CMP PFX.

This is the standard approach currently followed for CRM-to-Olympus.


WINDOWS / ONE-LINE COMMAND:

keytool -importkeystore -srckeystore CertAndKey.pfx -srcstoretype PKCS12 -destkeystore cacerts.jks -deststoretype JKS


Git Bash/Linux formatting:

keytool -importkeystore \
-srckeystore CertAndKey.pfx \
-srcstoretype PKCS12 \
-destkeystore cacerts.jks \
-deststoretype JKS


The command will request:

Source keystore password:
<PFX password>

Destination keystore password:
<JKS password>


After successful completion, the following file is created:

cacerts.jks


WHY WE CREATE THE JKS DIRECTLY FROM PFX

CMP has already generated the approved application certificate and matching
private key.

Therefore the correct flow is:

CMP
 |
 v
CertAndKey.pfx
 |
 v
keytool -importkeystore
 |
 v
cacerts.jks


There is no requirement to first download another generic JKS and import the
CMP certificate into that keystore.


